rgins  Abutting along the medial aspect of the scarred area is a somewhat well demarcated indurated gray white lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  This lesion comes to 1 7cm of the anterior and greater than 2 5cm of the posterior margin  Sectioning of the medial breast tissue reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm well circumscribed gray white fibrous nodule which comes to 1 4cm of the posterior and 1 1cm of the anterior margin The remaining mammary tissue shows diffuse dense nodular gray white fibrous tissue throughout  No other mass lesions or other gross abnormalities are identified  Sectioning of the upper outer quadrant reveals several tan red areas which may represent lymph node  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Entire gray white fibrous stellate scar submitted from lateral to medial with closest deep margin as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved fibrous tissue lateral to scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Indurated lesion abutting medial edge of fibrous scar   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Closest deep margin to indurated lesion in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative uninvolved fibrous tissue medial to scar and lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Well defined fibrous nodule in medial breast tissue to anterior and posterior margins   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue from upper outer quadrant which may represent lymph node  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1   RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION  2   LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART D  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART E  CRYOSTAT FRO