Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  04 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 26 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM  FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU ADJACENT TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  BLOOD VESSEL AND LYMPHATIC INVASION IS NOT SEEN  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 43                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of breast with a probe marking a mass on the radiograph  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 5cm tan  fleshy  firm  well circumscribed parenchymal nodule which comes within 0 1cm from the closest inked margin grossly  The nodule is entirely submitted in cassettes A and B  The remainder of the specimen is submitted in cassettes C through G  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  DANIELLE ELLIOTT  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST PARENCHYMAL NODULE  SUSPICIOUS FOR CARCINOMA  AWAIT PERMANANT  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION   report_end  , Unchecked.
