Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 AUG 94 ACCESSIONED ON  26 AUG 94 at 09 36 CLINICAL DATA  Pre menopausal staging  the patient has atrophic endometrium  History of breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1 INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  85    AND INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  15    MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  2 FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  NOTE  The tumor extends to an inked resection margin  frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  ENDOCERVIX  CURETTAGE  SQUAMOUS METAPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ENDOMETRIUM  CURETTAGE  REACTIVE ENDOMETRIUM  ENDOCERVICAL GLANDS WITH SQUAMOUS METAPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D  Signed On  31 AUG 94 at 16 32 Consulting Pathologist s   WANDA M  SZYFEKBEIN MD                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast mass  are two fragments of breast tissue  The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  it is inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue without specific lesions  It is submitted entirely in cassette I through L  The second measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  and is remarkable for a stellate retracted hard  scirrous area  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 2cm stellate hard white to tan nodule grossly involving the resection margin  A representative section of the nodule is frozen as frozen section  1  and kept frozen for Cox 5  The main nodule is submitted in cassette A through D and the remainder of this portion of tissue is submitted in cassette E through H  Received fresh in two separate parts  each  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number and as follows  The first container labeled  Endocervical curettings  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 0 3cm aggregate of soft  tan pink fragments of tissue  with a small amount of mucoid material admixed within  The specimen is wrapped and submitted entirely as M  The second container  labeled  Endometrial curettings  consists of a 2 x 1 x 0 3cm aggregate of red brown minute fragments of soft tissue  which are submitted entirely as N  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST MASS   INFILTRATING AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  Najmosama Nikrui  M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST MASS PART B  ENDOCERVIX  CURETTAGE PART C  ENDOMETRIUM  CURETTAGE   report_end  , Unchecked.
