 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left superior breast  two lesions   are two pieces of tissue  The largest tissue is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and contains a 2 2cm firm tan mass with infiltrative borders  Representative section of the mass are frozen as FX 1 and saved frozen  Tumor approaches ink  Representative sections of the larger tissue are submitted in cassettes A through C  The smaller REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm specimen contains two tan yellow  firm masses 1 0cm in diameter each  with infiltrative margins  Lesion entirely submitted in cassettes D through F  Normal breast are submitted in G through H  Received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  left breast mass  inferior wire  is a 3 x 3 x 1cm fragment of breast tissue with localizing wire  Specimen inked and sectioned to reveal a fir