Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 31 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO THE INFERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   SEE NOTE  Note  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN  POSTERIOR INFERIOR   INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO A MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  SEE NOTE  Note  The tumor extends to a margin away from the one marked by a suture  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN  POSTERIOR LATERAL   LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LYMPH NODE  LEFT AXILLA  HOT SPOT CT  363   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL 1   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN TWELVE OF TWELVE LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA  LEVEL 2   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN THREE OF THREE LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 12                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 06 49 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of breast with a long stitch marking the lateral margin  The short stitch marking the superior margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white stellate firm tumor mass  The tumor is abutting the inferior medial resection margin  0 5cm to the deep margin and 1 5cm to the superior and lateral margins  The remaining tissue is fibrofatty  A section of the tumor is frozen as frozen section  1  and resubmitted in cassette A  Tumor with inferior medial margin in B and C  Tumor with medial and deep margins in D  tumor with deep margin in E  Representative section of the remaining tissue in F and G  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axilla  hot spot  Ct 363  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan lymph node bisected and submitted entirely in cassette H  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary lymphadenectomy Level I  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm piece of yellow fatty tissue from which multiple tan pink lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 8cm are dissected away and submitted in its entirely in cassettes I through N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left axillary lymphadenectomy Level II  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of yellow fatty tissue from which two lymph nodes ranging in length from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm are dissected and submitted entirely in cassette O  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast additional posteroinferior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue with a stitch indicate the inferior margin  The specimen is inked as follows  The superior margin blue  deep margin green  medial margin red  lateral margin yellow  inferior margin black  The specimen is bisected  the half containing the superficial margin is submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes P through W  The piece containing the deep margin is submitted from medial to lateral in cassettes X through BB  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  additional posterolateral margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of yellow fatty breast parenchyma with a stitch to indicate the lateral margin  The lateral margin is inked green  the rest of the specimen is inked black  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes CC through HH  Resident  DAVID SABLE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE CARCINOMA O R  Resident  CHIN LEE WU  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Suzanne B  Keel  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL MARGIN  