or  the inferior margin in D  the superior margin in G  the posterior and the anterior margin in E  and the nipple in J   K L  representative sections of the second  lateral nodule M O  lymph nodes in axillary tail  largest four lymph nodes are bivalved and submitted in M and N   Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fibrofatty tissue which contains two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  The lymph nodes are submitted in cassette P  the larger lymph node is bivalved   Resident  Mari Mino  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LYMPH NODE  LEFT 1ST SENTINEL NODE   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  LYMPH NODE  LEFT 2ND SENTINEL NODE   METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA IN 1 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  O R  Resident  WEN JING  MD O R  Diagnosis by  GREGORY LAUWERS  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE LEFT SENTINEL  EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODE LEFT SENTINEL 2  EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY PART D  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILARY CONTENTS   report_end  , Checked.
