ned sequentially from posterior to anterior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm indurated  irregular and ill defined tan white mass which abuts the posterior and medial aspect  comes to within 0 9cm from the superior aspect  1 0cm from the inferior aspect and 2 2cm from the lateral aspect  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is composed of 85  tan yellow blue stained lobulated adipose tissue and 15  dense white fibrous tissue  No additional discrete masses or lesions are identified  Representative sections are sequentially submitted from posterior to anterior in cassettes A H with the posterior aspect in cassette A  the anterior aspect in cassette H and the entire ill defined mass in cassettes B D  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left axillary sentinel lymph node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm irregular portion of tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  which contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink lymph node  The lymph node is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette I  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast shaved margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm irregular portion of tan yellow to pink lobulated fibrofatty tissue with a suture designating the surface furthest from the tumor  The sutured aspect is inked black  the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm indurated tan pink firm area located on the non inked aspect and comes to within 0 3cm of the opposing black inked aspect  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is predominantly tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue with a minimum amount of dense white fibrotic tissue  The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially in cassettes J R with the indurated area in cassette L M  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left final deep margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm irregular tan