e sections from the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right breast   is a 17 x 13 x 2 5cm oriented right mastectomy specimen  The anterior surface contains a REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned along the medial to lateral axis to reveal a 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 1cm firm white mass located in the central to upper outer quadrant  The mass has a white to yellow cut surface and is 4 5cm to the closest posterior margin and 1 0cm to the closest anterior margin  The remaining breast parenchyma contains abundant amount of tan white rubbery fibrous tissue with soft yellow material present in the ducts suggestive of caseous necrosis  No additional discrete mass or lesion is noted  No lymph nodes are present  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of mass to closest anterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of mass to surrounding parenchyma   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cross section of nipple  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN and  right axillary contents   is an 11 x 3 x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  Twelve candidate lymph nodes are identified ranging in greatest dimension from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1 candidate lymph nodes   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   3 candidate lymph n