Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 31 CLINICAL DATA  Bilateral calcifications                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  60   AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU   40   FOCALLY COMEDO TYPE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Tumor is present in 2 slide  F and H  and the infiltrating component measures 0 5cm in greatest dimension  No definite vascular invasion is present  The infiltrating carcinoma is less than 0 1cm to the inked surgical margin Microcalcifications are seen  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  FIBROSIS  APOCRINE METAPLASIA  CYST AND MULTIPLE MICROCALCIFICATION  Diagnosis by  Christophe Girardet  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  Some cells of the in situ carcinoma stain for progesterone receptor protein  but the invasive cells fail to stain for this protein  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 16 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab in two separately labeled parts  Labeled  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire in place  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in A through I  Labeled  Right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue  inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  Submitted entirely in J through R  Resident  Metin Ozdemirli  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  PART A  LEFT BREAST PART B  RIGHT BREAST   report_end  , Unchecked.
