AL SMALL CALCIFICATIONS  3  RADIAL SCAR  4  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor size  Involving 7 of 10 blocks  Grade  3  Calcifications  In the carcinoma in situ and in benign changes  Margin of ductal carcinoma in situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to 0 2cm from the inked margin of the specimen in one focus  BREAST  LEFT  SUBAREOLA MASS    EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  SMALL FOCUS OF SEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS  LOCATED  0 1 CM FROM THE MARGIN  2  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MACROCYST AND CALCIFICATIONS  NOTE  Cautery artifact focally limits complete evaluation  Multiple levels examined  BREAST  LEFT  SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   BREAST  LEFT  LATERAL MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  INFERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL MARGIN    EXCISION  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  FAN  MD Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13 12                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block Z   Both ductal and lobular carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  Both ductal and lobular carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  