tibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 08 08 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch indicating the superior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral aspect of the specimen  The specimen is inked and sectioned superiorly to inferiorly to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm ill defined  tan gray firm area  0 2cm from the posterior margin  1 2cm from the medial margin  and 1 0cm from the lateral margin  In addition  the lesion is 0 5cm from the inferior margin and 0 5cm from the anterior margin  as well as 0 7cm from the superior margin  Representative sections of the tumor in relation to the posterior margin are submitted in cassettes A and B  Representative sections of the lateral resection margin are submitted in C  Representative sections of the superior margin are in D  Representative sections of the inferior margin submitted in cassette E  Representative sections of the anterior margin are submitted in cassette F  Labeled  axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue from which numerous lymph nodes are dissected and submitted in cassettes G through I  Labeled  add